[Opening "Queen's Gambit Declined"]

{Queen's Gambit Declined. Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.}
1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Be7 5. e3 h6 {Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.} 6. Bxf6 Bxf6 7. Nf3 O-O 8. cxd5 ! exd5 {Here the exchange is tempting and wrong: trading the good bishop leaves the dark squares bare.} (8... e5 Rb1 exd4 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qb3 c6 10. Bd3 Qb6 11. Qc2 Be6 ?! 12. O-O Nd7 13. h3 Be7 14. a3 Qc7 15. Rac1 Rac8 16. Bh7+ Kh8 17. Bd3 Bd6 18. Nd2 Nf6 19. f4 Qd8 20. Nf3 c5 21. Ne5 Kg8 22. Qf2 a6 23. Qf3 Rc7 24. Kh2 b5 25. Ne2 c4 26. Bc2 a5 27. Nc3 Rb7 28. e4 dxe4 29. Bxe4 Rb6 30. Bc6 b4 31. axb4 Rxb4 32. Rf2 Qb6 33. Rd1 Rxb2 34. Rxb2 Qxb2 35. d5 Bf5 36. Nxc4 Bxf4+ 37. Qxf4 Qxc3 38. Rd4 Rd8 39. d6 Bd7 40. Bxd7 Nxd7 41. Ne3 Kh7 42. Qe4+ g6 43. Qf4 Kg7 44. Qg3 Kf8 45. Qh4 Kg7 46. Qg3 Rc8 47. Re4 Kg8 48. Re7 Rd8 49. Qf4 Qf6 50. Qxf6 Nxf6 51. Nc4 a4 52. Ra7 Ne4 53. Rxa4 Nxd6 54. Nxd6 Rxd6 55. g3 Rd2+ 56. Kg1 Rd5 57. Kg2 f6 58. Ra7 h5 59. h4 Rd2+ 60. Kf3 Rd4 61. Ke3 Rg4 62. Kf3 Rd4 63. Ke3 Rc4 64. Re7 Rc3+ 65. Kf4 Ra3 66. Rb7 Ra4+ 67. Kf3 Ra2 68. Re7 Kf8 69. Rh7 Ra3+ 70. Kf4 Ra4+ 71. Kf3 Ra3+ 72. Kf4 Ra5 73. Rb7 Rf5+ 74. Ke4 Re5+ 75. Kf4 Rf5+ 76. Ke4 Re5+ 77. Kf4 Re7 78. Rb6 Kf7 79. Ra6 Rc7 80. Ra4 Kg7 81. Rb4 Ra7 82. Rb6 Ra4+ 83. Kf3 Ra3+ 84. Kf4 Ra4+ 85. Kf3 g5 86. hxg5 fxg5 87. Rb7+ Kf6 88. Rb6+ Kg7 89. Rb7+ Kg6 90. Rb6+ Kf5 91. Rb5+ Kg6 92. Rb6+ Kf5 93. Rb5+ Kf6 94. Rb6+ Kf7 95. Rb7+ Ke6 96. Rb6+ Kf7 97. Rb7+ Ke6 98. Rb6+ {The endgame is winning but not simple — the passed pawn needs its king, not just its rook.} Kf5 1/2-1/2

