[Opening "French Defense: Winawer Variation, Poisoned Pawn Variation, Main Line"]

{French Defense: Winawer Variation, Poisoned Pawn Variation, Main Line. Book so far. The plan is the usual one: finish development, then decide which side to open.}
1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. e5 c5 5. a3 Bxc3+ {A slight inaccuracy in move order — the bishop is better placed before this pawn commits.} 6. bxc3 Ne7 7. Qg4 Qc7 8. Qxg7 ! Rg8 {Prophylaxis. The move looks slow, and it takes away every active idea the opponent had.} (8... c4 Rb1 a5 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Qxh7 cxd4 10. Ne2 Nbc6 11. f4 dxc3 ?! 12. Qd3 d4 13. Nxd4 Nxd4 14. Qxd4 Bd7 15. Rg1 Nf5 16. Qf2 Qc6 17. Bd3 Qd5 18. Rb1 Bc6 19. Rb3 O-O-O 20. Rxc3 Kb8 21. g4 Nd4 22. Rg3 Qh1+ 23. Qf1 Nf3+ 24. Kf2 Qxh2+ 25. Qg2 Qxg2+ 26. Rxg2 Ne1 27. Rg3 Nxd3+ 28. cxd3 Rh8 29. Bd2 Rd5 30. Ke3 Rh2 31. g5 Be8 32. Be1 b6 33. Rc4 a5 34. Rd4 Rxd4 35. Kxd4 Kc7 36. Ke3 Rh1 37. Ke2 Rh2+ 38. Bf2 Rh1 39. Kd2 b5 40. Kc3 Rc1+ 41. Kb2 Rd1 42. Kc3 Rc1+ 43. Kd2 Rh1 44. Rg1 Rxg1 45. Bxg1 Bc6 46. Ke3 b4 47. axb4 axb4 48. Kd2 Bf3 49. Bc5 b3 50. Ba3 Bh5 51. Kc3 Bg6 52. Kxb3 Bxd3 53. Bc1 Bf5 54. Kb4 Bh7 55. Kc5 Kd7 56. Ba3 Bg6 57. Bb4 Be4 58. Kb5 Bd3+ 59. Kc5 Bg6 60. Ba3 Bf5 61. Bb4 Bd3 62. Bd2 Ke7 63. Kc6 Ke8 64. Bb4 Bf5 65. Ba3 Bb1 66. Bc5 Kd8 67. Kd6 Bh7 68. Bb6+ Ke8 69. Ba5 Bc2 70. Bb4 Bf5 71. Ba3 Kd8 72. Bb4 Ke8 73. Bc5 Bb1 74. Be3 Kd8 75. Bb6+ Ke8 76. Kc7 Bd3 77. Kd6 Bc2 78. Be3 Kd8 79. Bd4 Bh7 80. Bb6+ Ke8 81. Bc5 Kd8 {Precise to the end. A pawn move here instead would have let the defence build a fortress.} 82. Bb6+ 1/2-1/2

