[Opening "Ruy Lopez: Morphy Defense, Caro Variation"]

{Ruy Lopez: Morphy Defense, Caro Variation. Both sides have what they wanted from the opening. The middlegame will be about the centre.}
1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 a6 4. Ba4 b5 5. Bb3 Bb7 {Theory ends about here. From this point the game is decided by understanding rather than memory.} 6. c3 Nf6 7. Ng5 d5 8. exd5 ! Na5 {The point of the whole plan. Material is level, but only one side has a target to attack.} (8... b4 Na3 bxa3 {was the alternative — playable, but it hands over the initiative.}) 9. Bc2 Qxd5 10. f3 c5 11. O-O O-O-O ?! 12. Kh1 Qd7 13. b4 h6 14. Ne4 cxb4 15. cxb4 Nxe4 16. fxe4 Bxb4 17. a4 Kb8 18. axb5 Qxb5 19. Rf3 Qc5 20. Ba3 Nc6 21. Bb3 f5 22. Bd5 a5 23. Rc3 Qd4 24. Bxc6 Bxc6 25. Rxc6 Qxa1 26. Rb6+ Kc7 27. Ra6 Rxd2 28. Qc1+ Bc3 29. Qg1 Rf2 30. Qd1 Bd2 31. Bd6+ Kd7 32. Ba3 Kc7 33. Ra7+ Kb6 34. Rd7 Rc8 35. Kg1 Qa2 36. Rd6+ Ka7 37. Rd7+ Kb6 38. Rd6+ Ka7 39. Rd7+ {Resignation is timely: the king cannot be defended and the counterplay is one move too slow.} Kb6 1/2-1/2
